    "content": "The College Basketball Crown (CBC) is a new annual post-season men’s college basketball tournament launched in 2025 by FOX Sports and AEG. Held in Las Vegas, it features top-tier teams from major conferences (Big Ten, Big 12, Big East) that did not qualify for the NCAA Tournament, offering significant Name, Image, and Likeness (NIL) prize money for participants. Key Details About the College Basketball Crown: Structure: Inaugurated in 2025 as a 16-team tournament, the 2026 edition is an eight-team, single-elimination format, according to USA Today. USA Today Venue & Time: It is held on the Las Vegas Strip, specifically at T-Mobile Arena and MGM Grand Garden Arena, generally occurring from late March to early April. Purpose: The tournament serves as a premier alternative to the NIT, aiming to feature high-level competition and provide NIL opportunities for players, with a $500,000 prize pool in 2026, says USA Today. USA Today Participating Conferences: The tournament focuses on schools from the Big 12, Big Ten, and Big East, along with at-large participants. Inaugural Winner: The Nebraska Cornhuskers won the first tournament in 2025. Broadcast: All games are televised on FOX and FS1. The tournament is designed to thrive in the current landscape of college athletics, addressing the desire for competitive, high-stakes games for teams missing the NCAA tournament, notes Sportico. Sportico",
